        "cooked": "<aside class=\"quote group-playtesters\" data-username=\"lynkfox\">\n<div class=\"title\">\n<div class=\"quote-controls\"></div>\n<img loading=\"lazy\" alt=\"\" width=\"24\" height=\"24\" src=\"https://forums.greaterthangames.com/user_avatar/forums.greaterthangames.com/lynkfox/48/1997_2.png\" class=\"avatar\"> lynkfox:</div>\n<blockquote>\n<p>Not technically - The Operative is a Villain Character card. She just doesnt have her own setup. And each of the Enneads is a Villain Character card.</p>\n</blockquote>\n</aside>\n<p>She is a villain card and a character card, but she lacks the villain keyword, which would make her a Villain Character Card.</p>\n<p>&nbsp;</p>\n<p>Edit: Super awesome link that has Christopher even say Operative is not a Villain Character Card.&nbsp;<a href=\"https://greaterthangames.com/comment/5106#comment-5106\" rel=\"noopener nofollow ugc\">https://greaterthangames.com/comment/5106#comment-5106</a></p>",
